# 6. ROUTING ENGINE

This is the most important component.

Build four primary routing modes.

## A. AUTO ROUTING

Automatically choose the most appropriate configured provider and model.

Consider:

- Model capability
- Task type
- Provider availability
- Latency
- User-defined priority
- Configured cost preferences
- Rate limits
- Context window
- Tool calling requirements

Allow the owner to configure routing rules.

Example:

Simple task -> Fast model

Coding task -> Coding-capable model

Complex reasoning -> Reasoning-capable model

Vision task -> Vision-capable model

Do not claim to understand task complexity perfectly. Provide transparent rule-based routing first and optional AI-based classification later.

## B. MANUAL ROUTING

Allow selecting an exact:

- Provider
- Model
- Model alias

The selected provider must be used unless an explicitly enabled fallback policy applies.

## C. COMBO ROUTING

Allow creating custom routing groups.

Each combo includes:

- Combo Name
- Description
- Primary Provider
- Secondary Providers
- Ordered Provider List
- Routing Strategy
- Model Mapping
- Retry Rules
- Timeout Rules
- Enabled / Disabled

Support these strategies:

### Sequential Combo

Try providers in configured order.

Example:

Provider A -> Provider B -> Provider C

Move to the next provider when a retryable failure occurs.

### Parallel Combo

Send requests to multiple providers concurrently.

Allow configurable response-selection strategies:

- First successful response
- First complete response
- Preferred provider response
- Lowest-latency eligible response

Make parallel requests optional because they can increase API costs.

Cancel unnecessary requests when possible.

Never treat an incomplete streamed response as a successful complete answer.

### Weighted Load Balancing

Distribute requests according to configurable weights.

Example:

Provider A: 50%

Provider B: 30%

Provider C: 20%

Provide configurable distribution and health-aware exclusion.

### Priority Routing

Try providers based on configured priority and availability.

Allow the owner to edit priority without changing provider configurations.

